        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Trump sending US delegation for Iran talks in Pakistan Middle East Issued on: 19/04/2026 - 17:30 Modified: 19/04/2026 - 17:32 US President Donald Trump said US negotiators will head to Pakistan on Monday for another round of talks with Iran, raising hopes of extending a fragile ceasefire set to expire by Wednesday even as Washington and Tehran remain in a standoff over the Strait of Hormuz. There ⁠is ​currently ​no decision by Iran to ​send ‌a ⁠negotiating ‌delegation to ⁠Pakistan \"as long as there ​is ‌a naval blockade,\" ‌Iran's ​Tasnim news agency reported on Sunday. Douglas Herbert, FRANCE 24's international affairs commentator tells us more. 'Ceasefire in the Middle East, especially in Lebanon, are meant to be broken', analyst says 19/04/2026 Middle East Iran asserts leverage in Hormuz ahead of new round of talks 19/04/2026 Middle East Israel's double game between negotiations with Lebanon and occupation in the south 19/04/2026 Middle East Food security under threat as Middle East war disrupts fertiliser supply 19/04/2026 Middle East A petition called 'Lebanon will not be the next Gaza' calls on French leaders to take action 19/04/2026 Middle East Iran: Prolonged conflict reshapes view of the regime, analyst says 19/04/2026 Middle East Middle East: Hezbollah blamed after French peacekeeper killed in Lebanon 19/04/2026 Middle East What is UNIFIL? the UN mission in southern Lebanon explained 19/04/2026 Middle East Strait of Hormuz: Open, closed, open, closed - What's actually happening? 18/04/2026 Middle East"
